Data Source

Source of Strain Data

All gravitational-wave strain data and event metadata used by this repository are retrieved from the Gravitational Wave Open Science Center (GWOSC).

The pipeline uses:

GWOSC event metadata to obtain GPS timestamps

Open strain data accessed via GWPy TimeSeries fetch utilities

Network and Caching Behavior

The first execution may take longer due to network downloads of strain data. Subsequent runs may benefit from local caching, depending on environment configuration.

If a cache directory is configured and writable, downloaded data may be reused across runs.

Data Integrity Expectations

All event identifiers used correspond to publicly listed GWOSC events. If data for a specific event or detector is unavailable, the script logs the error and continues processing remaining events.

Detector Coverage

By default, the analysis processes data from the H1 (Hanford) and L1 (Livingston) detectors. The detector list can be modified in the script configuration.

Event List Notes

The event list includes canonical gravitational-wave detections, multiple catalog versions where applicable, and selected special entries where available. The analysis treats all event names as catalog keys and does not rely on astrophysical classification.
